---
import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/marketing/SiteNav.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/marketing/Colophon.astro';
import { docsPrefix } from '../data/doc-versions.mjs';

// scripts/stage-esp32-firmware.mjs writes this at deploy time when a release
// carries the K-Touch build. Its absence means none does yet.
const MANIFEST_URL = '/flash/esp32/ktouch/manifest.json';
const manifestFile = join(process.cwd(), 'public', MANIFEST_URL);
const firmware = existsSync(manifestFile) ? JSON.parse(readFileSync(manifestFile, 'utf8')) : null;

// The ESP32 install guide first ships in the 1.1 docs, wherever 1.1 is served.
const GUIDE = `${docsPrefix('1.1')}/installation/#esp32-touchscreen-btt-k-touch---alpha`;
const link = 'text-secondary underline underline-offset-2';
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="Flash a K-Touch - HelixScreen"
  description="Install the HelixScreen firmware on a BigTreeTech K-Touch from your browser over USB."
>
  <SiteNav />
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight mb-3">Flash a K-Touch from your browser</h1>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-3 max-w-[62ch]">
      This writes the HelixScreen firmware onto a BigTreeTech K-Touch over USB, with no Python or
      esptool to install. The panel then joins your WiFi and talks to your printer's Moonraker.
      Nothing is installed on the printer.
    </p>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-10 max-w-[62ch]">
      The ESP32 build is an alpha: expect rough edges and missing features. It replaces the
      K-Touch's stock firmware.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl mb-3">You need</h2>
    <ul class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-10 max-w-[62ch] list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>A BigTreeTech K-Touch</li>
      <li>A USB-C cable that carries data (some charge-only cables don't)</li>
      <li>Chrome or Edge on a desktop computer. Other browsers and phones can't open a serial port.</li>
      <li>
        On Windows, the CH340 USB driver from WCH if no new COM port appears when you plug the panel in.
        Linux and recent macOS have it built in.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl mb-3">Install</h2>
    {firmware ? (
      <div class="mb-10">
        <script is:inline type="module" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/esp-web-tools@10.4.0/dist/web/install-button.js"></script>
        <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-4 max-w-[62ch]">
          Plug the K-Touch in, switch it on, then press the button and pick its port
          (usually named USB Serial or CH340).
        </p>
        <esp-web-install-button manifest={MANIFEST_URL}>
          <button slot="activate" type="button" class="btn btn-strong">
            Install HelixScreen <span class="tabular">{firmware.version}</span>
          </button>
          <p slot="unsupported" class="ui text-sm text-ink max-w-[62ch]">
            This browser can't talk to USB serial devices. Open this page in Chrome or Edge on a
            desktop computer, or follow the <a href={GUIDE} class={link}>command-line install</a>.
          </p>
          <p slot="not-allowed" class="ui text-sm text-ink max-w-[62ch]">
            Flashing needs a secure (https) page. Open
            <a href="https://helixscreen.org/flash/" class={link}>helixscreen.org/flash</a>.
          </p>
        </esp-web-install-button>
        <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mt-4 max-w-[62ch]">
          The installer offers to erase the device first. A first install over the stock
          firmware should erase. To update a panel already running HelixScreen, leave
          "Erase device" unchecked: that keeps its WiFi network and settings.
        </p>
      </div>
    ) : (
      <p class="ui text-sm text-ink mb-10 max-w-[62ch]">
        No ESP32 build is published yet. It arrives with the 1.1 releases; until then, see the
        <a href={GUIDE} class={link}>install guide</a>.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2 class="text-xl mb-3">After it restarts</h2>
    <ol class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted mb-10 max-w-[62ch] list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>
        The panel broadcasts its own WiFi hotspot named <span class="font-mono">HelixScreen-XXXX</span>.
        Join it from your phone or computer; it has no password.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open the address shown on the panel (normally <span class="font-mono">http://192.168.4.1</span>)
        and enter your WiFi network, its password and your printer's Moonraker host.
      </li>
      <li>Tap Connect. The panel joins your network and connects to the printer.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="ui text-sm text-ink-muted max-w-[62ch]">
      There is no on-screen setup wizard on the K-Touch. Recovery, backing up the stock firmware
      and what doesn't work yet are in the <a href={GUIDE} class={link}>full install guide</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Colophon />
</MarketingLayout>
